IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-disclosures`
IMPORT `pid-protections`
IMPORT `pid-dealing`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in pid-disclosures.l4,
-- pid-protections.l4 and pid-dealing.l4. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- Dates are illustrative. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

-- Short names for the kinds of disclosure.
`voluntary` MEANS `a voluntary public interest disclosure`
`deemed` MEANS `a voluntary public interest disclosure by determination of the head of an agency`
`witness` MEANS `a witness public interest disclosure`
`mandatory` MEANS `a mandatory public interest disclosure`
`not a PID` MEANS `not a public interest disclosure`

`head` MEANS `the head of an agency`
`officer` MEANS `another disclosure officer for an agency`
`manager` MEANS `my manager`
`minister` MEANS `a Minister or a member of a Minister's staff`
`MP` MEANS `a member of Parliament who is not a Minister`
`journalist` MEANS `a journalist`
`elsewhere` MEANS `someone else`

`own accord` MEANS `of my own accord`
`code` MEANS `because a code of conduct told me to`
`role` MEANS `in meeting the ordinary requirements of my role or functions`
`obligation` MEANS `under a statutory or other legal obligation`
`asked` MEANS `at the request of, or as required by, someone investigating serious wrongdoing`

`corrupt` MEANS `corrupt conduct`
`other matter` MEANS `something else`

-- Helper A: a public official, not a member of Parliament, reporting a non-trivial matter they honestly believe shows
-- serious wrongdoing, no grievance, in writing; s 28 facts all favourable; the earlier disclosure on 15 January 2025
-- and this one on 1 January 2026.
GIVEN `to` IS A `To whom I made the disclosure`, `how` IS A `How I came to make the disclosure`, `official` IS A BOOLEAN, `about` IS A `What my disclosure is about`, `wilful` IS A BOOLEAN, `det` IS A BOOLEAN, `rev` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The kind of disclosure`
`kind A` `to` `how` `official` `about` `wilful` `det` `rev` MEANS
    `What kind of public interest disclosure did I make` `official` FALSE `about` FALSE `how` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `to` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) `wilful` `det` `rev`

-- Helper B: s 26 content, to a disclosure officer, of own accord.
GIVEN `belief` IS A BOOLEAN, `policy` IS A BOOLEAN, `grievance` IS A BOOLEAN, `sig` IS A BOOLEAN, `rma` IS A BOOLEAN, `arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The kind of disclosure`
`kind B` `belief` `policy` `grievance` `sig` `rma` `arises` MEANS
    `What kind of public interest disclosure did I make` TRUE FALSE `corrupt` FALSE `own accord` `belief` `policy` `grievance` `sig` `rma` `arises` `officer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Helper C: s 28, a disclosure to a member of Parliament or a journalist.
GIVEN `to` IS A `To whom I made the disclosure`, `true` IS A BOOLEAN, `earlier` IS A BOOLEAN, `anon` IS A BOOLEAN, `waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `told` IS A BOOLEAN, `received` IS A BOOLEAN, `day earlier` IS A DATE, `review` IS A BOOLEAN, `day this` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The kind of disclosure`
`kind C` `to` `true` `earlier` `anon` `waived` `told` `received` `day earlier` `review` `day this` MEANS
    `What kind of public interest disclosure did I make` TRUE FALSE `corrupt` FALSE `own accord` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `to` FALSE `true` `earlier` `anon` `waived` `told` `received` `day earlier` `review` `day this` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Helper D: the maker and the manner (s 25, s 24(3)(c)).
GIVEN `mp` IS A BOOLEAN, `to` IS A `To whom I made the disclosure`, `orally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The kind of disclosure`
`kind D` `mp` `to` `orally` MEANS
    `What kind of public interest disclosure did I make` TRUE `mp` `corrupt` FALSE `own accord` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `to` `orally` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 14 -- public official`

#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am employed in or by an agency, or otherwise in its service` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I have public official functions that an integrity agency is authorised to investigate` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am an individual in the service of the Crown` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am a statutory officer` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I provide services or exercise functions for an agency, including as a contractor, subcontractor or volunteer` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I work for an entity engaged to provide services or exercise functions for an agency, and am involved in that work` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am a judicial officer` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am a member of Parliament or a Minister` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am employed under the Members of Parliament Staff Act 2013` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `none of these` `the regulations say nothing about me` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(2): the regulations decide either way.
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `none of these` `the regulations declare me to be a public official` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a public official` `I am employed in or by an agency, or otherwise in its service` `the regulations declare me not to be a public official` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 13 -- serious wrongdoing`

#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `corrupt conduct` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `corrupt conduct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the government information or state records Acts` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a contravention of a pecuniary interest obligation under the Local Government Act 1993 or a council code of conduct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `administrative conduct of an agency or public official that is unlawful, unreasonable, unjust, oppressive, improperly discriminatory or based on improper motives` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a failure by an agency or public official to act in accordance with the privacy or health records Acts` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `a serious and substantial waste of public money` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what I am reporting serious wrongdoing` `something else` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 21-29 -- the kind of disclosure: recipients, occasions, determinations`

-- Helper A arguments: to, how, public official, about, wilfully false, determination, revoked.
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind A` `officer` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind A` `manager` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
-- s 27: no listed recipient.
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 29: a determination makes it voluntary "even if"; revoked, it falls away from the start.
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `deemed`
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 21(2): wilfully false; with an unrevoked determination it stays deemed (fork F2).
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `own accord` TRUE `corrupt` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `deemed`
-- s 25: not a public official.
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `own accord` FALSE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 23: mandatory (role, legal obligation); a code of conduct is not a legal obligation (s 23(2)).
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `role` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mandatory`
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `obligation` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `mandatory`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `code` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `code` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- Not about serious wrongdoing: not mandatory; s 26 turns on the honest belief, held here, so voluntary.
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `role` TRUE `other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
-- Mandatory needs a public official; so does voluntary.
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `role` FALSE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 22: a witness need not be a public official; wilfully false, not a PID; a determination does not change a witness
-- or mandatory disclosure (fork F2).
#ASSERT `kind A` `elsewhere` `asked` FALSE `corrupt` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `witness`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `asked` TRUE `other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `witness`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `asked` TRUE `corrupt` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `asked` TRUE `corrupt` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `witness`
#ASSERT `kind A` `head` `role` TRUE `corrupt` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`

-- Helper D arguments: member of Parliament, to, orally. s 25; s 24(3)(c).
#ASSERT `kind D` FALSE `minister` FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind D` FALSE `minister` TRUE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind D` FALSE `head` TRUE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind D` TRUE `head` FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`

§§ `s 26 -- content`

-- Helper B arguments: belief, policy only, grievance only, significant implications, disagreement with reasonable
-- management action, arises from an earlier disclosure.
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind B` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 26(4): a grievance arising from an earlier disclosure is not excluded.
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind B` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `voluntary`

§§ `s 28 -- members of Parliament and journalists`

-- Earlier disclosure 15 January 2025: the 6 months end 15 July 2025; from 16 July 2025. With internal review: 15
-- January 2026; from 16 January 2026. 31 August 2025: end 28 February 2026, from 1 March 2026. 31 August 2023 (leap
-- year next): end 29 February 2024, from 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS `d` 16 7 2025
#ASSERT `From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` (`d` 15 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS `d` 16 1 2026
#ASSERT `From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` (`d` 31 8 2023) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 3 2024
#ASSERT `From what day may I go to a member of Parliament or a journalist` (`d` 31 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS `d` 1 9 2026

-- Helper C arguments: to, substantially true, earlier same disclosure, earlier anonymous, waived, told of s 55(3)
-- decision, received required information, day of earlier, internal review, day of this.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 16 7 2025) EQUALS `voluntary`
#ASSERT `kind C` `MP` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 16 7 2025) EQUALS `voluntary`
-- The last day of the period: (e)(i) not yet met.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 15 7 2025) EQUALS `not a PID`
-- (e)(ii) a s 55(3) decision notified: any time.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) EQUALS `voluntary`
-- Internal review: 12 months.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 16 7 2025) EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 16 1 2026) EQUALS `voluntary`
-- The required information was received.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
-- (a)-(d) each failing.
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind C` `journalist` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
#ASSERT `kind C` `MP` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `not a PID`
-- s 28 does not apply to a disclosure to the head of an agency.
#ASSERT `kind C` `head` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 16 1 2025) EQUALS `voluntary`

§§ `s 32 -- detrimental action`

#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `injury, damage or loss caused to me` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `damage to my property` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `damage to my reputation` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `intimidation, bullying or harassment` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `unfavourable treatment in my career, profession, employment or trade` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `discrimination, prejudice or adverse treatment` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `disciplinary proceedings or disciplinary action` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `some other disadvantage` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `a threat of any of these, express or implied` `none of these` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `nothing that disadvantaged me` `none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `disciplinary proceedings or disciplinary action` `a lawful investigation of serious wrongdoing or other misconduct` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `damage to my reputation` `the lawful reporting or publication of a finding, or lawful adverse comment, resulting from such an investigation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it detrimental action` `injury, damage or loss caused to me` `a prosecution for a criminal offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 31 -- reasonable management action`

-- Arguments: kind, action reasonable, way reasonable, corrupt, to conceal, suspected disclosure contributed, to reduce risk.
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 31(4)(d): all three limbs; taken to reduce the risk, it can still be reasonable management action.
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `management action of a kind listed in section 31(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `it was not management action` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `some other management action` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was it reasonable management action` `some other management action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

